    "author_association": "NONE",
    "body": "### Contributing guidelines\n\n- [x] I have read [CONTRIBUTING.md](https://github.com/nvim-mini/mini.nvim/blob/main/CONTRIBUTING.md)\n- [x] I have read [CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md](https://github.com/nvim-mini/mini.nvim/blob/main/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md)\n\n### Module(s)\n\nmini.completion\n\n### Description\n\nPreviously the default `vim.o.complete` of '.,w,b,u,t' would cause slowdowns in mini-completion, even if the user didn't use ctags.\n\nA workaround was added to remove `t` unless user explicitly sets it via eb4d6bd268f7168a8a0d187c93d5954d5ef93bfd\n\nThe source of the problem was the vim.lsp.tagfunc erroneously sending synchronous LSP requests during the insert completion, it has been fixed here: https://github.com/neovim/neovim/pull/37260\n\nMaybe the workaround could be guarded with a `nvim-0.12` check? It is strange to have to set the already-default options for tag completion to work as a fallback.",
    "closed_at": null,
    "closed_by": null,
    "comment_data": [
        {
            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "> The source of the problem was the vim.lsp.tagfunc erroneously sending synchronous LSP requests during the insert completion, it has been fixed here: [neovim/neovim#37260](https://github.com/neovim/neovim/pull/37260)\n\nThanks for the suggestion!\n\nI am not if this specifically was the root cause, so will have to verify that Nightly doesn't have the performance issues. But even then, I think it might be reasonable to keep the behavior:\n- If the slowness is due to `textDocument/definition` request, then it means there is LSP attached. This also usually means that there is a regular LSP step with `textDocument/completion` requests from 'mini.completion'. I don't think it is common to have `textDocument/completion` request fail and `textDocument/definition` succeed (i.e. to actually get to the fallback step).\n- It doesn't have to be \"... have to set the already-default options for tag completion to work as a fallback.\". It can be a `vim.o.complete = vim.o.complete` before `require('mini.completion').setup()`. This technically qualifies as \"set before `setup()`\" and the option value shouldn't be changed.",
