            "author_association": "NONE",
            "body": "> * If the slowness is due to `textDocument/definition` request, then it means there is LSP attached. This also usually means that there is a regular LSP step with `textDocument/completion` requests from 'mini.completion'. I don't think it is common to have `textDocument/completion` request fail and `textDocument/definition` succeed (i.e. to actually get to the fallback step).\n\nFWIW, I think the case triggered fairly easily when using mini-snippets LSP for an oddball filetype (markdown file in large java repo). For my setup completion \"fails\" if no snippet matches for such filetypes. Then i saw a strange error about \"no servers supporting textDocument/definition\" and knew my answer as to why it was slow.",
